Food production and Nutrients (@farming-nutrition: 0, #part-of @farming, #contains @farming-food-identity, #contains @farming-prepared-foods, #contains @farming-dairy-foods, #contains @farming-nonfarm-inputs, #contains @saccharomyces-cerevisiae, #farming-practice @farming-dairy-foods, #farming-practice @farming-food-identity, #farming-practice @farming-nonfarm-inputs, #farming-practice @farming-prepared-foods, #farming-practice @saccharomyces-cerevisiae) { r_6K5MKDYYSKVCXVYQE2YJDXGG2W
Nutrients.lingua is the supporting food dataset: 463 measured food preparations from TACO and USDA. The Farming species Records link to it with #related-food. That relationship means relevant production context; it does not prove the exact species, cultivar, recipe, or nutrient composition of another harvest.

Keep raw, cooked, canned, dried, milled, fermented, salted, and oil-extracted food entries separate. Water loss, processing, added ingredients, edible bones, and the measured portion can change values substantially. A crop's kg yield is not automatically kg of the edible preparation.

Use @solanum-lycopersicum to learn tomato production, then select the actual raw tomato or tomato-product Record for nutrition. Use @gallus-gallus-domesticus for poultry husbandry, then choose egg, liver, breast, or another measured preparation. No nutrient numbers are copied or assigned as universal species properties.

Every existing food is associated with a species production example, a prepared-food category, an unresolved-identity category, or non-farm inputs. Ambiguity remains visible until the original sample or a supplier provides evidence.
} r_6K5MKDYYSKVCXVYQE2YJDXGG2W

