| Food name | Check before using a species method |
| --- | --- |
| Abóbora and pumpkin seed, unspecified | Several Cucurbita species and hybrids. Compare @cucurbita-pepo, @cucurbita-maxima, and `@cucurbita-moschata`. |
| Abobrinha paulista | Often @cucurbita-moschata; verify the cultivar rather than assuming all zucchini are `@cucurbita-pepo`. |
| Acelga | Chinese cabbage can be @brassica-rapa; true chard is `@beta-vulgaris`. |
| Alfavaca | Several Ocimum species. Compare @ocimum-gratissimum and `@ocimum-basilicum`. |
| Banana cultivar names | @musa-acuminata ancestry or @musa-acuminata-balbisiana hybrid groups; verify clone and nursery identity. |
| Café | @coffea-arabica, @coffea-canephora, or a blend. An infusion's measured dilution is part of its food identity. |
| Canola oil | Food-quality canola can involve @brassica-napus, @brassica-rapa, or other approved cultivar backgrounds; oil name alone does not prove species. |
| Cará and inhame | @dioscorea-alata and other Dioscorea yams versus @colocasia-esculenta taro. Names vary by region. |
| Caruru | Several Amaranthus species; @amaranthus-viridis is an identified production example. |
| Cebolinha | Often @allium-fistulosum, but chives or young @allium-cepa can share the name. |
| Chicória | Often @cichorium-endivia, sometimes other chicories; almeirão/catalonha commonly use `@cichorium-intybus`. |
| Erva-doce | @foeniculum-vulgare or @pimpinella-anisum; confirm the ingredient. |
| Feijão broto | Often @vigna-radiata, sometimes @glycine-max or another pulse; obtain edible-sprouting identity and safe seed. |
| Jabuticaba | @plinia-cauliflora is one species; several Plinia species supply the food. |
| Jambo | @syzygium-jambos is one identity; red jambo can be @syzygium-malaccense or another Syzygium. |
| Jamelão | Commonly @syzygium-cumini; verify identified stock before planting. |
| Kiwi | @actinidia-deliciosa is one food species; green, gold, and hardy Actinidia differ. |
| Laranja-lima | Often a low-acid @citrus-sinensis cultivar in Brazil; the market name needs confirmation. |
| Mexerica Murcott | Usually a tangor hybrid with mandarin and sweet-orange ancestry; not proof of pure `@citrus-reticulata`. |
| Mostarda | Several Brassica species; compare @brassica-juncea and `@brassica-rapa`. |
| Pera Park and unspecified ameixa | Confirm cultivar and species before using @pyrus-communis or @prunus-salicina instructions. |
| Serralha | @sonchus-oleraceus is one edible identity; confirm the plant. |
| Taioba | Use an identified edible @xanthosoma-taioba clone; related ornamentals are not interchangeable food. |
| Tremoço | Several Lupinus species and sweet/bitter cultivars; compare @lupinus-albus only after identification. |
| Tucumã | @astrocaryum-aculeatum and A. vulgare have different identities and production contexts. |
| Wheat flour and pasta | @triticum-aestivum, @triticum-turgidum-durum, or blends; retain the actual ingredient identity. |

Some clearly conventional names have a #related-food edge to their usual crop despite this remaining uncertainty. That edge is navigational context, not a taxonomic determination of the sample.
