| Cuscuz de milho | @zea-mays; salt and additions depend on the measured preparation. |
| Cuxá | Vinagreira is commonly @hibiscus-sabdariffa; rice, sesame, shrimp, and other ingredients depend on the dish. |
| Charuto de repolho, quibebe | @brassica-oleracea or the identified Cucurbita cultivar; fillings and additions vary. |
| Feijão tropeiro, feijoada, virado | @phaseolus-vulgaris with recipe-dependent cassava/maize flour, pork, egg, and greens. |
| Frango com açafrão | @gallus-gallus-domesticus; identify the actual seasoning, often @curcuma-longa in Brazil rather than true saffron. |
| Macarrão à bolonhesa | Wheat, @solanum-lycopersicum, and usually @bos-taurus; proportions vary. |
| Maniçoba, tucupi, tacacá | @manihot-esculenta with dish-specific processing; tacacá often also uses @acmella-oleracea and shrimp. A crop Record is not a safe detoxification recipe. |
| Tabule | Wheat, @solanum-lycopersicum, @petroselinum-crispum, and recipe-dependent herbs and additions. |
| Tapioca with butter, vaca atolada | @manihot-esculenta and usually @bos-taurus; confirm the measured food's ingredients. |

A dish association does not authorize copying its nutrient totals to any one ingredient. Weigh the actual edible harvest and select or calculate the actual preparation separately.
