Dairy preparations (@farming-dairy-foods: 0, #part-of @farming-nutrition, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-261, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-262, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-448, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-449, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-461, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-462, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-463, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-464, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-467, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-469, #related-food @nutrition-br-fdc-171284, #related-food @nutrition-br-fdc-170886, #related-food @nutrition-br-fdc-170887) { r_3XABP2G1T8E5CN97NQW2JB20JT
Milk explicitly labelled de vaca links to @bos-taurus; milk explicitly de cabra links to `@capra-hircus`. Unspecified yoghurt, cheese, and butter remain prepared dairy foods. Cattle provide a common production example, but the product label and original measurement determine the milk species, fat content, ingredients, and process.

Use @farming-animal-products for milking, cooling, pasteurization, and hygiene. Yoghurt fermentation, cheese curd/whey separation, butter churning, milk concentration, and UHT processing change the food and its composition. A live animal's feed requirement or milk yield does not describe the nutritional value of a particular cheese.
} r_3XABP2G1T8E5CN97NQW2JB20JT

Salt and drinking water (@farming-nonfarm-inputs: 0, #part-of @farming-nutrition, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-517, #related-food @nutrition-br-fdc-173647) { r_77WYY2PPRP6Y9P7WM81V1VD6PJ
Coarse salt is a mineral product; potable tap water is treated drinking water. Neither has a planting or livestock lifecycle. Salt extraction, water treatment, and laboratory verification are separate production processes. Use potable water for harvest washing and food processing; suitability for irrigation alone does not establish drinking-water quality.
} r_77WYY2PPRP6Y9P7WM81V1VD6PJ

Baker's yeast — Saccharomyces cerevisiae (@saccharomyces-cerevisiae: 0, is #species, #part-of @farming-nutrition, #related-food @nutrition-br-taco-514, #source @farm-source-yeast) { r_6ZEHAD7FZGFDN1Y26Z4BD7XYKX
A cultivated fungus used in biological baker's yeast, not a plant seed or livestock species. Cells multiply mainly by budding under appropriate culture conditions. Food production starts with a defined clean strain, controlled substrate, temperature, aeration, and contamination checks; biomass is then separated and sold fresh or dried by the producer's process.

For household baking, use a food-grade commercial culture and the recipe's hydration and fermentation conditions. Gas production raises dough; baking completes the food process. Keep fresh yeast cold as labelled, protect dry yeast from moisture, and replace inactive or contaminated stock. A sourdough starter is a mixed microbial community and does not inherit the compressed-yeast tablet's nutrient measurements.
} r_6ZEHAD7FZGFDN1Y26Z4BD7XYKX
